            0.198,
            0.847,
            0.271
          ],
          "content": "2. A cube has 11 possible net structures in total. In this count, two nets are considered the same if one can be obtained from the other by a rotation or a flip. For example, the following nets are all considered the same —"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
